Riley Queen from Poly Haven (https://polyhaven.com/a/chess_set), included
unmodified (the glTF, its buffer, and its three diffuse textures in
scenes/models/chess/textures/; its normal and roughness maps are not
included). It
has been dedicated to the public domain under Creative Commons CC0 1.0
Universal and is not covered by the Apache License.

scenes/models/apollo/apollo_lunar_module.glb and astronaut.glb are from NASA's
3D Resources (https://github.com/nasa/NASA-3D-Resources, "Apollo Lunar Module"
and "Astronaut"), which NASA offers free and without copyright. The lunar
module is included unmodified; the astronaut was written back out without its
Draco compression by tools/gltf_decompress.py and its arms lowered by
tools/pose_astronaut.py. scenes/models/apollo/lm5_eagle.glb is the lunar
module modified by tools/make_lm5_eagle.py (decoded, faces regrouped into
named parts, normals worked out, struts shortened, scaled, panels given
texture coordinates, and written without compression), with the panel
textures lm5_eagle_panels.png and lm5_eagle_rivets.png that tool draws.
NASA does not endorse this project. The comparison images of NASA photographs
AS11-40-5903 and AS11-40-5927 (Neil Armstrong) in docs/images/changelog/ and
docs/images/ are NASA images, in the public domain.

scenes/terrain/apollo11_inner.glb, apollo11_outer.glb and
apollo11_inner_crop.tif were made by tools/geotiff_terrain.py from the Lunar
Reconnaissance Orbiter Camera's Narrow Angle Camera digital terrain model of
the Apollo 11 landing site, NAC_DTM_APOLLO11 (product
NAC_DTM_APOLLO11_E008N0234, 2 m posting; https://pds.lroc.im-ldi.com),
courtesy NASA/GSFC/Arizona State University, in the public domain: cropped
around Tranquility Base, its middle 9 m flattened, and tessellated.
scenes/terrain/apollo11_inner_albedo.png and apollo11_outer_albedo.png were
made by tools/geotiff_albedo.py from the orthoimages released with that model,
NAC_DTM_APOLLO11_M150361817_50CM and NAC_DTM_APOLLO11_M150361817_2M (from LROC
NAC frame M150361817), courtesy NASA/GSFC/Arizona State University, in the
public domain: cropped, the sunlight's shading divided out with the model, the
lunar module and its shadow painted over, and normalized.
scenes/terrain/apollo11_surroundings.hdr is Ray's render of those meshes
(scenes/terrain/apollo11_bake.ray). The source model and orthoimages
themselves are not included.
NASA and ASU do not endorse this project.

